    "sha": "ee42f9b2e9e3638144e1c2d61d6d5fb831e6064c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKGVlNDJmOWIyZTllMzYzODE0NGUxYzJkNjFkNmQ1ZmI4MzFlNjA2NGM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T23:30:50Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T23:30:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pick): refuse face-normal alignment on an inside-out or open body\n\nFace outward normals for the plane lay (one face or two edges) and the\n3-2-1 work-offset alignment came from the facets' winding with no check\nthat the winding is the solid's outside: an inside-out STL laid the part\nupside down silently. pick::winding now judges each body (connected\nfacets over welded edges, 1e-4 mm spatial-hash weld): closed and\nconsistently wound with positive signed volume (divergence theorem) is\ntrusted; inside-out, open, non-manifold, mixed-winding or zero-volume\nbodies refuse the pick by face and part name. Nothing mutates the\nuser's geometry. Verdicts are memoized in a bounded thread-local MRU\nkeyed by an ordered, winding-sensitive content hash.\n\nPinned by winding_align (inverted cube refuses the face lay, the\ntwo-edge lay and the 3-2-1; the outward cube still aligns; open,\nmixed and non-manifold bodies refuse; bodies judged one by one; the\nshipped test models read outward; testdata/models/cube_inside_out.stl\nreads inside-out).\n\nFixes #366\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
